      "A": "Own storage and copy-cost research in src/tropical.cpp. Use 75da56ed78a5455d as the starting candidate: retain contiguous signed-integer matrices, exact initialization and exclusion semantics. Separately evaluate selective const-reference passing and locally owned partition moves from c1879ded1a614be1; that bundle's slower standalone result does not establish whether its individual changes help the contiguous layout. Preserve mutable DFS-history ownership, partition LIFO order and child insertion order. Never retain references into partitions across vector growth or removal. Deliver separable, measured changes rather than assuming all allocation reductions should be combined.",
      "B": "Own Prim selection and redundant-work research. Retain e0b493a50bd34fbd as a measured candidate; compare its two-pass minimum/first-match selection with a simple const-reference single-pass scan. Preserve the lowest-index tie, selected-key invalidation, visited relaxation guard and -1 result when no eligible finite key exists. Investigate removing cycle checks and their matrix only with a general equivalence proof: committed arcs connect earlier-selected parents to selected children, while a tentative arc enters an unselected vertex; account explicitly for directed matrix writes, rollback and the parent[u] > 0 condition. Do not substitute a conventional MST implementation, since inclusion constraints and tie behavior affect later paths. Preserve spanning-edge order and failure behavior. Keep the cycle-elimination experiment separate from the measured selector change.",
      "C": "Own deterministic path-search and parallelism research. Start from 2375758088364796, but compare its root-summary implementation with threading disabled through the same serial execution path: the observed improvement could come from shared immutable graph access rather than parallel work. Preserve serial root-zero search, ascending-root result commitment and completion of every earlier root needed before accepting a later success. Cancellation must not discard an earlier potential winner. Evaluate the ordered adjacency and incremental color-count kernel from 9c7870b88b47431f separately, with private traversal state per worker. Preserve stored-edge neighbor order, leaf-only evaluation, original nCores stopping target and strict-greater fallback updates. Gate threading by general workload characteristics within the existing four-core allowance. Treat sibling-partition parallelism from 84e69104e3ef481b as a lower-priority alternative, not an additional nested parallel layer.",
      "G": "Integrate actual programs supplied by the research trees, inspecting complete implementations rather than relying on the truncated displayed diffs. Preserve 75da56ed78a5455d as the provisional best standalone fallback. Within the unchanged measurement budget, prioritize its combination with B's measured selector, then its combination with C's root-search implementation; attempt the three-way combination only if supported by remaining budget and pairwise evidence. Add newly validated copy reductions or cycle elimination individually. Resolve overlapping graph-reference and traversal changes explicitly. For parallel variants, keep mutable scratch private and commit results in reference order; sibling generation must retain insertion order because partitions are consumed LIFO. Require unchanged-oracle correctness and a whole-input equivalence argument before accepting speed results. Compare complete integrated programs against their constituents: a slower combination must be rejected even when each ingredient helped separately. Keep tests, oracle, compiler, target, permissions and budgets unchanged.",
      "analysis": "The relevant workload is Problem A's tropical-path implementation, not the other contest problems. Baseline mean is 8.521 ms; the leading standalone candidates are A's contiguous matrices at 5.277 ms, C's ordered root search at 5.283 ms and B's selector at 5.375 ms, approximately 1.6x baseline speed. Their small differences do not establish a reliable ranking: baseline samples span 7.223–10.869 ms, candidate dispersion is unavailable, and no integrations were measured. Sibling parallelism, broad copy removal and incremental DFS measured 6.468, 7.078 and 7.123 ms respectively, so they are hypotheses for selective reuse rather than automatic additions. Source-level opportunities include repeated deep copies, cycle-check work and repeated path scans; timing data do not identify their individual costs or prove that parallel regions executed. Exact path choice depends on traversal, tie and partition order, not merely the final color count. Four baseline correctness cases cannot establish correctness for every valid input."
